{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers","id":1022430,"title":"Kinfolk Sorcerers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-26T13:00:01-08:00","id":1022430,"title":"Kinfolk Sorcerers","content":"I had a question concerning Kinfolk Sorcerers. Let us say that you have a male Human Garou Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 who learned how to transform into a wolf using the Numina of Shapeshifting. Could they breed with female wolves and produce Wolf Kinfolk and Lupus Garou puppies? The same question could be applied in reverse with a male Wolf Kinfolk who learned how to transform into a human using the Numina of Shapeshifting, could they breed with female humans and produce Human Garou Kinfolk and Homid Garou children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:11:17-08:00","id":1022505,"title":"","content":"I'd say Yes to all of them, but I've always been in the &quot;Well, it looks pretty wrong/OP/ridiculous, but as long as it makes a good story...&quot; camp when it comes to mediating edge cases like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:21:51-08:00","id":1022511,"title":"","content":"Sounds squick to me but if you want magic dudes to fuck wolves and make more Kinfolk in your game, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T18:30:58-08:00","id":1022566,"title":"","content":"I would plainly say &quot;yes&quot;. If this transformation is good enough to procreate, it is good enough to procreate with Garou. And since the Kinfolk status is a spiritual phenomenon, I see no reason for that to not work.<br /> <br /> Do it at your discretion, and play with possibilities and consequences as you please, there is a lot of room for things going pretty weird at that level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T20:33:01-08:00","id":1022601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers#post1022430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I had a question concerning Kinfolk Sorcerers. Let us say that you have a male Human Garou Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 who learned how to transform into a wolf using the Numina of Shapeshifting. Could they breed with female wolves and produce Wolf Kinfolk and Lupus Garou puppies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Though, unlike Garou who are half wolf, you are literally just having a human have sex with canines. There is a very decent chance that the Pure Breed doesn't come through, given that it is entirely mystical and you are undergoing a magical transformation. This could go either way though, depending on ST preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers#post1022430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The same question could be applied in reverse with a male Wolf Kinfolk who learned how to transform into a human using the Numina of Shapeshifting, could they breed with female humans and produce Human Garou Kinfolk and Homid Garou children?</div> </div> </div> </div>How are you wolves learning magic to shapeshift? They're wolves. So I would say no, this doesn't work.<br /> <br /> This entire line of thought reeks of bestiality. Again, at least with Garou they are half-human, half-wolf (and half spirit) so the crossbreeding doesn't strike me as being quite as odd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022566#post1022566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would plainly say &quot;yes&quot;. If this transformation is good enough to procreate, it is good enough to procreate with Garou. And since the Kinfolk status is a spiritual phenomenon, I see no reason for that to not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spiritual nature of it is why I would say it very well might not work. There is no way to account for that spiritual aspect to come through intact through the magical transformation. I'm not dead set against the idea, but it could certainly fail because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-26-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T21:45:13-08:00","id":1022612,"title":"","content":"I am thinking that it may be an emergency way for Tribes that are about to lose the Wolf to anchor their lineage with a new group of wolves. While Kinfolk Sorcerers are rare, they are probably not as rare as Garou, so they could be used to procreate among animal populations to create new Wolf Kinfolk lineages while Garou are fighting the good fight. Of course, most of them might find the idea to be revolting, but there may be a few willing to 'think of Gaia' and get the job done. <br /> <br /> As for Wolf Kinfolk learning Numina, I am unaware of any rule that forbids Animal Kinfolk from learning Numina if they belong to Animal Kinfolk groups that have sufficient intelligence (Ajaba, Bastet, Corax, Garou [including Hakken], Gurahl, Kitsune, and Nuwisha [the write ups of the Ananasi, Mokole, Nagah, Rokea, and Ratkin seem to suggest that their Animal Kinfolk are not bright enough, but that would really be up to the ST]). While the Shapeshifting Path from Revised is externally focused (it allows you to transform other people into animals for goodness sake), the Shapeshifting Path from Hedge Wizard is internally focused and, from the descriptions of the Path in Hedge Wizard, could be one of the few Paths that should be adaptable to Animal Kinfolk. Of course, it is up to the individual STs whether they want Animal Kinfolk Sorcerers running around, but I think that it would definitely add a mythic quality to a game to have animals learning to transform into humans (though I would personally have them use the required Willpower roll to maintain their memories of being animal and to avoid being permanently locked into a human form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T23:06:41-08:00","id":1022627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022612#post1022612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Wolf Kinfolk learning Numina, I am unaware of any rule that forbids Animal Kinfolk from learning Numina if they belong to Animal Kinfolk groups that have sufficient intelligence (Ajaba, Bastet, Corax, Garou [including Hakken], Gurahl, Kitsune, and Nuwisha [the write ups of the Ananasi, Mokole, Nagah, Rokea, and Ratkin seem to suggest that their Animal Kinfolk are not bright enough, but that would really be up to the ST]). While the Shapeshifting Path from Revised is externally focused (it allows you to transform other people into animals for goodness sake), the Shapeshifting Path from Hedge Wizard is internally focused and, from the descriptions of the Path in Hedge Wizard, could be one of the few Paths that should be adaptable to Animal Kinfolk. Of course, it is up to the individual STs whether they want Animal Kinfolk Sorcerers running around, but I think that it would definitely add a mythic quality to a game to have animals learning to transform into humans (though I would personally have them use the required Willpower roll to maintain their memories of being animal and to avoid being permanently locked into a human form).</div> </div> </div> </div>It... it just smells like an excuse for animals to bang humans and vice-versa. A Lupus kin being a sorcerer in the first place is already pretty incredible (and actually interesting, handled sparingly), but then to use that magical talent to fuck human women while disguised just seems super-duper weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T06:34:32-08:00","id":1022720,"title":"","content":"Well, let us ignore the interspecies breeding (despite it being a core part of the Fera) and talk about Animal Kinfolk Sorcerers. Which Paths do you think they would be capable of learning? I think that they could definitely develop Psychic Numina, definitely could not develop Scientific Numina, and could develop some Paths of Mythic Numina. I think that Alchemy, Conjuration, and Enchantment (from either Hedge Wizard or Revised) would be impossible to learn unless they already could transform into humans. <br /> <br /> I would suggest changing the rules making every Animal Kinfolk except Rat Kinfolk and Spider Kinfolk sapient when they reach sexuality maturity (the books are pretty clear that those two types are intelligent but not sapient) and, when they reach sexuality maturity, give them equivalent lifespans of Human Kinfolk unless their animal species innately possesses a superior lifespan. Otherwise, your Wolf Kinfolk Sorcerers would have only an average of ten years of adventuring in them. Of course, they could have a Flaw that limits them to the normal lifespan of the mundane members of the species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T06:47:17-08:00","id":1022724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022612#post1022612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Wolf Kinfolk learning Numina, I am unaware of any rule that forbids Animal Kinfolk from learning Numina if they belong to Animal Kinfolk groups that have sufficient intelligence (Ajaba, Bastet, Corax, Garou [including Hakken], Gurahl, Kitsune, and Nuwisha [the write ups of the Ananasi, Mokole, Nagah, Rokea, and Ratkin seem to suggest that their Animal Kinfolk are not bright enough, but that would really be up to the ST]).</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cite where the books say that these animal kinfolk are of human intelligence? You are the first person I have ever heard make that argument, so I'm curious where it comes from.<br /> <br /> Edit: The only example I know of offhand is the &quot;Caged Folk&quot;, unverified Ratkin kinfolk inspired by the Rats of NIMH (which is one of the Fera you say don't get intelligent kinfolk).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-27-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T07:15:15-08:00","id":1022739,"title":"","content":"The fact that you can play Wolf Kinfolk without any restrictions beyond those experienced by Red Talon Kinfolk suggests that they are sapient (Unsung Heroes, p. 48). Heck, if you wanted to spend the freebie points, you could have a Wolf Kinfolk that was as good a scientist as Einstein (Intelligence 5 and Sciences 5), though you would need one of your Garou relatives to transcribe your research papers and to speak at conferences for you. Since the rules do not forbid Wolf Kinfolk Physicists, I do not particularly see why they would forbid Wolf Kinfolk Sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T07:44:11-08:00","id":1022752,"title":"","content":"While I don't think animals can learn Numina, I do think they would be effected by it. A wolf turned human would be amusing. <br /> <br /> However, the Path, as written, is for temporary changes. Even if the change occurs on the genetic level, when it reverts, there goes the pregnancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:01:04-08:00","id":1022782,"title":"","content":"The Hedge Wizard version of Shapeshifting is different from the Revised version of Shapeshifting because Hedge Wizard is a crossover book while Revised is a Mage book. I would use the crossover book for Kinfolk rather than the Mage book, as Animal Kinfolk Sorcerers would be more of a Werewolf thing than a Mage thing. In any case, it would not matter for male Kinfolk fertilizing females of the appropriate species, since the sperm is independent after it is released. Of course, no one is saying you have to allow Animal Kinfolk Sorcerers, I am just saying that they are not specifically forbidden by the existent rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:16:57-08:00","id":1022821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022782#post1022782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, no one is saying you have to allow Animal Kinfolk Sorcerers, I am just saying that they are not specifically forbidden by the existent rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually their are rules which actually state the opposite. If you are familiar with the Skull Pigs from the guide to the Wyrm, then you are aware that they were once kinfolk to the Grondr and they can gain the intelligence and skills necessary to caste Sorcery. These Voodoo Pigs are pretty much what you are talking about just you want to make them wolves and justify their powers through another source.<br /> <br /> Lets also not forget that Wolves can be Kami, and Kami are not restricted from learning Numina. So a wolf or human Kami could learn not only the Shape shift Sorcery but they could simply learn to shape shift the way Fera do. If they happen to also be kinfolk with pure breed they do not lose that and should in fact have it carry on as normal regardless of what form they are in when the procreate as long is it is relevant to the species they are kin to.<br /> <br /> That said, I would expect that the elders are going to be against the act entirely. Going outside the norms and using Sorcery is going to gain notoriety from most of the tribes. Going against what you are is also deviant behavior as noted by the fact that Garou can lose renown for acting to much outside their own Auspice. Since Kinfolk are judged more harshly then full members of the tribe I would expect that this type of behavior judged equally if not more harshly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:22:45-08:00","id":1022826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022739#post1022739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you can play Wolf Kinfolk without any restrictions beyond those experienced by Red Talon Kinfolk suggests that they are sapient (Unsung Heroes, p. 48). Heck, if you wanted to spend the freebie points, you could have a Wolf Kinfolk that was as good a scientist as Einstein (Intelligence 5 and Sciences 5), though you would need one of your Garou relatives to transcribe your research papers and to speak at conferences for you. Since the rules do not forbid Wolf Kinfolk Physicists, I do not particularly see why they would forbid Wolf Kinfolk Sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So starting by saying that I'm not trying to be difficult here. I just want to make sure I understand your stance on this. In your games (and actually in your view of how the WoD in general functions), at least half, sometimes more of the populations (those that are kinfolk) of wolves (Garou), hyenas (Ajaba), big cats (Bastet), ravens (Corax), bears (Gurahl), foxes (maybe just Asian foxes)(Kitsune) and coyotes (Nuwisha) are fully sentient and capable of not only human intelligence, but human levels of genius intelligence?<br /> <br /> And all of this, even though the books that discuss lupus characters (and animal form characters in general) make sure to explain that around the time of the First Change the character goes through a mental awakening where they come into their human intellect?<br /> <br /> I think the idea of a unique animal kinfolk with higher intelligence is interesting enough. But you are presenting it like it's the norm. Mostly (as far as I can tell) based on 2 or 3 paragraphs of rules that don't specifically disallow it. Am I missing something? (I am sincerely trying to understand)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:45:31-08:00","id":1022904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022821#post1022821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually their are rules which actually state the opposite. If you are familiar with the Skull Pigs from the guide to the Wyrm, then you are aware that they were once kinfolk to the Grondr and they can gain the intelligence and skills necessary to caste Sorcery. These Voodoo Pigs are pretty much what you are talking about just you want to make them wolves and justify their powers through another source.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems illogical. 1. This isn't a general 'kinfolk of various species or breeds can learn magic' rule. 2. Skullpigs are not a good example of why untainted kinfolk wolves could learn sorcery. Their ability to become smart enough to intentionally do evil is specifically said to be a work of the Wyrm. The Skullpigs are more like a mockery breed like the Warwolves than anything else. Normal kinfolk animals don't behave that way or have the capacity to ever become that way.<br /> <br /> Even a Kami or Gorgon is going to behave far differently than just a smart wolf with sorcery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:10:19-08:00","id":1022915,"title":"","content":"Well, Animal Kinfolk are supernatural creatures because they can learn level one Gifts if they can find a suitable teacher and are capable of reproducing to create more Animal Kinfolk (and, in the case of everyone except the Corax and Ratkin, Fera), so they are not normal animals trying to do sapient things. The fact that White Wolf (and Onyx Path) never outlined the capabilities of Animal Kinfolk suggests that they have human intelligence (with the exception of Rat and Spider Kinfolk, where they specifically addressed the question of the intellectual capabilities of those types of Animal Kinfolk). While normal animals should probably not be able to learn Numina (unless you wanted to play a mythic campaign), I see nothing in the rules that forbids supernatural animals like Animal Kinfolk from learning Numina (like Human Kinfolk, Animal Kinfolk are mortal and supernatural, allowing them some of the benefits of both worlds). <br /> <br /> Kami are not a good comparison because any Possessed animals could develop Spirit Gifts, not just Animal Kinfolk, as their sapient nature is either derive from their possessing spirit or by Gaia directly awakening their spirit. You could play a Kami Butterfly if you wanted, it would gain substantial advantages over normal butterflies because it would effectively gain the capabilities of a human while retaining the shape of a butterfly. While most STs would probably fall over laughing if a player tried to have a Kami butterfly learn how to drive amotorcycle, there is no explicit rule against animals learning to drive motorcycles within cWoD (and that is actually a common circus act). I would suggest that most STs would give a four to eight dice penalty to such activities (four dice for a wolf, six dice for a snake, and eight dice for a butterfly).<br /> <br /> Yes, in some cases, that would mean that the majority of the surviving members of certain species would be Kinfolk that could learn potentially learn Numina. I would think that the Khan would be moving Heaven and Earth to teach their Tiger Kinfolk every trick under the Sun to keep them alive, so I would imagine that a greater percentage of Tiger Kinfolk would have Gifts and/or Numina than Wolf Kinfolk. Of course, if Kinfolk characters have the fourth level of the Shapeshifting (Hedge Wizard) Path, it is an academic question whether they are Human Kinfolk who learned to become animals or Animal Kinfolk who learned to become humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:38:14-08:00","id":1022958,"title":"","content":"I'd go with &quot;whatever works for your campaign&quot; <br /> <br /> My first thought, for example, is having the idea not work and the kin folk is actually diluting the bloodlines. So your pack has to track down the kin and convince them that they are not helping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:45:53-08:00","id":1023006,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, so the question I posed earlier then: In your view of canon, the majority of wolves, hyenas, and big cats, being kinfolk, are all fully sentient to human levels of intellect? And then a portion (since less of the animals probably belong to kinfolk families) of ravens, bears, foxes (at least Asian foxes) and coyotes are also fully sentient?<br /> Again, I am just trying to understand your view of the WoD. Moving from there (and if I misunderstood, please correct me), your reasoning for thinking such is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that White Wolf (and Onyx Path) never outlined the capabilities of Animal Kinfolk suggests that they have human intelligence </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-28-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:59:44-08:00","id":1023011,"title":"","content":"The only non-human animals who are sapient are Animal Kinfolk. Animal Kinfolk are intelligent enough to hide from the humans who would kill them, leaving their mundane cousins to bear the brunt of human deprivations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T16:07:15-08:00","id":1023015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022904#post1022904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems illogical. 1. This isn't a general 'kinfolk of various species or breeds can learn magic' rule. 2. Skullpigs are not a good example of why untainted kinfolk wolves could learn sorcery. Their ability to become smart enough to intentionally do evil is specifically said to be a work of the Wyrm. The Skullpigs are more like a mockery breed like the Warwolves than anything else. Normal kinfolk animals don't behave that way or have the capacity to ever become that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please note that I said that they would have to have to justify their powers through another source. I never said it was a general rule, only that the precedent had been set that animal kinfolk have in the past gained intelligence and learned sorcery. The same to your second point.<br /> <br /> I personally think that the whole premise of the OP's question if illogical. The idea of one or the other wanting to perform the act in question would be grotesque and unnerving in most instances. Just because a man takes the form of a wolf doesn't mean that the other wolves are going to view him like a wolf or that he will be able to communicate with them. His human conditioning since birth would tell him that what he is wanting to do it wrong because society has deemed so and just being able to transform isn't going to change that.<br /> <br /> Going with the OP's question however, I offered a potential avenue to explain this occurrence in his story if S/HE decide to go that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T11:19:01-08:00","id":1023355,"title":"","content":"Animal kinfolk who are intelligent and can learn Gifts and become Sorcerers is not how I would do it. But whatever works for your group.<br /> <br /> However, in the old Ways of the Wolf sourcebook, it does state that even normal wolves in the World of Darkness possess &quot;a certain degree of sentience&quot; as a result of their closer ties to Gaia. While not human intelligence, it is a kind of awareness and wisdom. As far as I know, this has not been repeated in other books or utilized in any scenario. It's probably just meant as a way to justify STs using wolves in a storytelling type way rather strictly by actual behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:13:49-08:00","id":1023396,"title":"","content":"Hm, you are right. I wonder if other animals who are associated with the Changing Breeds would have similar improvements in intelligence? Not the sapience of Animal Kinfolk (if you want to include that), but something better than we have in our world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:27:18-08:00","id":1023402,"title":"","content":"another question on Kinfolk Sorcery<br /> <br /> Ideas how to use the divination Numina<br /> <br /> ive got an idea for a prophecy, that a FBI agent investigating the death of a Police officer (Carried out by a kin via biting bullets) &quot;Knows without proof&quot; <br /> <br /> not sure how many dots of divination someone needs to form that kind of result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T15:28:58-08:00","id":1023457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1023355#post1023355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal kinfolk who are intelligent and can learn Gifts and become Sorcerers is not how I would do it. But whatever works for your group.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just it though (and what I was trying to wrap my head around). Aya Tari wasn't saying that this is how he/she runs it for their game. They are saying fully human intelligence kinfolk who can do that or more are completely canon as written (for everyone but the Ratkin and Ananasi).<br /> <br /> I had stated so previously, but I actually like this as a unique kinfolk idea. But the premise that there are a few hundred thousand (kinfolk across the different Fera) human intelligence animals running around the WoD (some of them learning/teaching sorcery) seems really far off of canon to me. Especially since the reasoning is &quot;well the game doesn't specifically forbid it&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1023402#post1023402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another question on Kinfolk Sorcery<br /> <br /> Ideas how to use the divination Numina<br /> <br /> ive got an idea for a prophecy, that a FBI agent investigating the death of a Police officer (Carried out by a kin via biting bullets) &quot;Knows without proof&quot;<br /> <br /> not sure how many dots of divination someone needs to form that kind of result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the kinfolk that's going to have the prophecy a PC? If not, then just do it. In Werewolf, you don't even need Numina to have prophetic visions. Otherwise, it's more important I think to figure out how far out the vision is (to figure out level) and clarity is then determined by successes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T16:43:41-08:00","id":1023487,"title":"","content":"Actually, the numbers would be probably around a million human-level intelligence Animal Kinfolk. They would just hide from humans. Of that amount, I would suggest that 1% would bother developing Numina and 0.1% would bother learning Gifts (probably the same percentage of the around six million Human Kinfolk). Of course, no ST has to use them, I just think it would be quite interesting to have crows and wolves who learn to become human and decide to take human wives for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T07:36:55-08:00","id":1025936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022739#post1022739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you can play Wolf Kinfolk without any restrictions beyond those experienced by Red Talon Kinfolk suggests that they are sapient (Unsung Heroes, p. 48). Heck, if you wanted to spend the freebie points, you could have a Wolf Kinfolk that was as good a scientist as Einstein (Intelligence 5 and Sciences 5), though you would need one of your Garou relatives to transcribe your research papers and to speak at conferences for you. Since the rules do not forbid Wolf Kinfolk Physicists, I do not particularly see why they would forbid Wolf Kinfolk Sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unsung Heroes seems to indicate otherwise in regards to 'Wolf Kinfolk Physicist.'<br /> &quot;They should allot their smallest portion to knowledges&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Allot the usual points in Attributes (6/4/3 in Physical, Social, and Mental Traits), but distribute the largest portion among Physical Attributes&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;For Abilities (Talents, Skills, and Knowledges), use a 7/3/1 distribution, taking the lowest number in Knowledges.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, while these generalizations about what goes on in an animal's head are largely conjecture, you have to start somewhere. Here are just a few things to consider when playing a wolf (or any nonhuman). Animals aren't stupid. Animals are as intelligent as they need to be. Can you say a wolf is stupid because it can't work long division or understand not to cross the street against the light? On the other hand, she would likely think humans are hopelessly inept because they would freeze or starve in her territory, completely oblivious to all that's obvious to her lupine awareness.<br /> <br /> The language seems clear in this regards that they don't have human intelligence. Just smart as an animal needs to be. And 'I spend all my points on intelligence and knowledge' seems, while not against the rules, clearly against the spirit of animal kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:34:59-08:00","id":1025987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1025936#post1025936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsung Heroes seems to indicate otherwise in regards to 'Wolf Kinfolk Physicist.'<br /> &quot;They should allot their smallest portion to knowledges&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Allot the usual points in Attributes (6/4/3 in Physical, Social, and Mental Traits), but distribute the largest portion among Physical Attributes&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;For Abilities (Talents, Skills, and Knowledges), use a 7/3/1 distribution, taking the lowest number in Knowledges.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, while these generalizations about what goes on in an animal's head are largely conjecture, you have to start somewhere. Here are just a few things to consider when playing a wolf (or any nonhuman). Animals aren't stupid. Animals are as intelligent as they need to be. Can you say a wolf is stupid because it can't work long division or understand not to cross the street against the light? On the other hand, she would likely think humans are hopelessly inept because they would freeze or starve in her territory, completely oblivious to all that's obvious to her lupine awareness.<br /> <br /> The language seems clear in this regards that they don't have human intelligence. Just smart as an animal needs to be. And 'I spend all my points on intelligence and knowledge' seems, while not against the rules, clearly against the spirit of animal kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I see it as well. It had never occurred to me to have animal kinfolk running around with human intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T14:46:26-08:00","id":1026172,"title":"","content":"I agree with Monalfie and idpersona, having wolf kinfolk be exceptionally smart<i> for a wolf</i> doesn't mean they are able to achieve human-level self-awareness. A solitary example of a wolf that possesses numina (and the wherewithal to use it) is interesting and mysterious. It is cool precisely because it never happens. The notion that there are a million hyper-intelligent wolves and that<i> ten thousand of them know sorcery</i>(!?!) seems game-altering and absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T15:53:59-08:00","id":1026192,"title":"","content":"Just quickly on a semi related tangent.<br /> The Breed/Birth Form of a Garou's Child depends on the Breed of the <b>Mother</b>, right?<br /> <br /> So, am I correct in assuming.<br /> <br /> Homid Garou Father X Normal Wolf Mother = Wolf Kinfolk<br /> Normal Wolf Father X Homid Garou Mother = Homid Kinfolk<br /> Lupus Garou Father X Normal Human Mother = Homid Kinfolk<br /> Normal Human Father X Lupus Garou Mother = Wolf Kinfolk<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T17:18:30-08:00","id":1026230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1026192#post1026192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just quickly on a semi related tangent.<br /> The Breed/Birth Form of a Garou's Child depends on the Breed of the <b>Mother</b>, right?<br /> <br /> So, am I correct in assuming.<br /> <br /> Homid Garou Father X Normal Wolf Mother = Wolf Kinfolk<br /> Normal Wolf Father X Homid Garou Mother = Homid Kinfolk<br /> Lupus Garou Father X Normal Human Mother = Homid Kinfolk<br /> Normal Human Father X Lupus Garou Mother = Wolf Kinfolk<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:52:04-08:00","id":1026404,"title":"","content":"This topic was hijacked from the oroginal topic into guessing the animal Kinfolk capabilities while not taking into account the OMEGA answer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1022752#post1022752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, the Path, as written, is for temporary changes. Even if the change occurs on the genetic level, when it reverts, there goes the pregnancy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With the matter reverting at least after the end of the spell the effect would be a &quot;not even a misscarriage&quot; - insufficient time to form a fetus.<br /> Hovever I'd specifically rule that any matter (hair, spit, semen, etc.) would revert into the original form when leaving the sorcerer's body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:25:20-08:00","id":1026499,"title":"","content":"Perhaps with the Path from Revised, but the Path from Hedge Wizard is permanent until reversed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:55:20-08:00","id":1026577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1026404#post1026404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic was hijacked from the oroginal topic into guessing the animal Kinfolk capabilities while not taking into account the OMEGA answer:<br /> <br /> With the matter reverting at least after the end of the spell the effect would be a &quot;not even a misscarriage&quot; - insufficient time to form a fetus.<br /> Hovever I'd specifically rule that any matter (hair, spit, semen, etc.) would revert into the original form when leaving the sorcerer's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, you aren't using the most powerful version of the Path written, from an earlier book, that got a Revised edition that fixed some of the brokenness of the rules. That's your fault for not cherry picking the wording/book that makes you the most powerful. (Hopefully the sarcasm was obvious)<br /> <br /> and...great signature <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:10:15-08:00","id":1026584,"title":"","content":"Well, the Hedge Wizard version does not allow you to transform Kindred into mice, so it is arguable which version is more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T20:39:33-08:00","id":1026838,"title":"","content":"oh another question? <br /> <br /> lets compare The Hedge Magic Numina &quot;Healing&quot; with the psychic numina &quot;Empathic Healing&quot;<br /> <br /> what are the reasons you see to take one or the other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:41:09-08:00","id":1026852,"title":"","content":"Well, a more apt comparison would be between Empathic Healing and Psychic Healing, as they are both Psychic Numina. Psychic Healing is capable of accomplishing rapid healing of bashing damage at level three (one bashing health level per success, one turn per bashing health level, no cost) and lethal damage at level four (one lethal damage per success, 10 minutes per lethal health damage healed, cost is one point of Willpower). Did I mention that a beginning Sorcerer character could easily start with Perception 5, Empathy 5, Medicine 5, Psychic Healing 5, Willpower 10, and the Merits of Ability Aptitude (Empathy) and Ability Aptitude (Medicine) and Wild Talent (Psychic Healing) 4, which would allow them to heal an average of seven health levels of bashing or lethal damage per roll? You would practically have to kill yourself using Empathetic Healing to do what you do what you can do with minimal time and effort with Psychic Healing.<br /> <br /> The only reason to take Healing is if you already favor Mythic Numina or Scientific Numina, as it is much less effective than Psychic Healing. If you want to lay a dedicated mortal healer (not that Garou really need one), you want to play a psychic with Psychic Healing. The strange thing is that there is nothing that would prevent a mortal with Psychic Healing from using it to heal Changelings, Ghouls, Kindred, Kinfolk, Mages, etc, as level three and level four allow the healer to use their powers to directly knit together flesh and bone, meaning that a highly skilled healer would be a very desirable commodity in the supernatural community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:55:19-08:00","id":1027059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1026584#post1026584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Hedge Wizard version does not allow you to transform Kindred into mice, so it is arguable which version is more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a version outside of WoD Sorcerer or Sorcerer Revised?<br /> <br /> Both of those lasted one scene. I do tend to house rule a 'duration' aspect in that would allow permanent changes at level 6, but that is just a house rule (and well into the realm of strange and bizarre possibilities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T08:58:22-08:00","id":1027064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1026838#post1026838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh another question? <br /> <br /> lets compare The Hedge Magic Numina &amp;quot;Healing&amp;quot; with the psychic numina &amp;quot;Empathic Healing&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> what are the reasons you see to take one or the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the same reason one would take Via Ignis over Hellfire or Pyrokinetics. Better fit for the character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:01:32-08:00","id":1027066,"title":"","content":"No, the Hedge Wizard version is a permanent change that must be reversed by another application of Shapeshifting or Unweaving Countermagic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:07:04-08:00","id":1027069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027066#post1027066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Hedge Wizard version is a permanent change that must be reversed by another application of Shapeshifting or Unweaving Countermagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking Sorcerer - The Hedge Wizard's Handbook? Just trying to understand the context of what the Hedge Wizard version means.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T12:09:17-08:00","id":1027200,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is the earlier version of Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:22:11-08:00","id":1027550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1026577#post1026577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...got a Revised edition that fixed some of the brokenness of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player &amp; also as a GM I always force to use the latest version (This also help to reduce misunderstandings in a troupe). Also I have an additional iron rule. If something can be (mis)understood in two different ways I always choose what is LESS beneficial to the players. This is the World of Darkness, for Gaia's sake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1026577#post1026577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and...great signature <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I had an unresistable urge to stole it. You started a movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:32:08-08:00","id":1027555,"title":"","content":"They are really two different powers that share the same name. The first is a power you can use only on yourself that can cause you to go insane. The second is a power that tums your enemies into mice and your allies into tigers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:30:54-08:00","id":1027591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027550#post1027550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As a player &amp; also as a GM I always force to use the latest version (This also help to reduce misunderstandings in a troupe). Also I have an additional iron rule. If something can be (mis)understood in two different ways I always choose what is LESS beneficial to the players. This is the World of Darkness, for Gaia's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good take on it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027550#post1027550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sorry, I had an unresistable urge to stole it. You started a movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Credit where credit is due, I lifted it from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2810_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2810\" data-vbnamecard=\"2810\">Yakecen-Sings</a> (with permission). Spread it far and wide though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027555#post1027555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are really two different powers that share the same name. The first is a power you can use only on yourself that can cause you to go insane. The second is a power that tums your enemies into mice and your allies into tigers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second is the Revised (literally) version of the first. Obviously, use whatever you want for your table, but to say that they are 2 different powers is disingenuous.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:05:40-08:00","id":1027622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027200#post1027200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is the earlier version of Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Lachdanan, I almost always just use the most current version of things. Kind of the intent of making reproductions of the newer gameline. Seems like a semi-moot point to ask how a power from, what, the 90's? Works in conjunction with the modern rules. I'm not sure what the rules for Pure Breed were back in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm still not sure I'd allow it without reading more into the power itself (since I don't have that book). The magic of a sorcerer, as far as I know, might not be the same that governs Garou. Looking like a wolf, and essentially being a wolf, doesn't necessarily cause whatever makes Garou to change as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:06:53-08:00","id":1027623,"title":"","content":"They have completely different effects though. The first gives a beginning character a substantial social bonus, the ability to substantually augment one physical attribute, and the ability transform into an animal (from a mouse to an elephant) with the risk of insanity. The second gives a beginning character the ability to transform into any animal that has ever existed (from a flea to a Giganotosaurus), two of their allies into any animal that has ever existed, or two of their enemies into any animal that has ever existed without any chance to resist if they do not know countermagic. Did I mention that the second version works equally well on supernatural creatures as mortals, so a beginning character could potentially turn Methuselahs into bugs and kill them by stepping on them because the Methuselahs will gain the Attributes and Health Levels of a bug (they will still have their Abilities, Blood Pool, and Disciplines, so they may be very hard bugs to kill depending on their Discipline spread, but they will have to survive for one scene as a bug)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:33:54-08:00","id":1027639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027623#post1027623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have completely different effects though. The first gives a beginning character a substantial social bonus, the ability to substantually augment one physical attribute, and the ability transform into an animal (from a mouse to an elephant) with the risk of insanity. The second gives a beginning character the ability to transform into any animal that has ever existed (from a flea to a Giganotosaurus), two of their allies into any animal that has ever existed, or two of their enemies into any animal that has ever existed without any chance to resist if they do not know countermagic. Did I mention that the second version works equally well on supernatural creatures as mortals, so a beginning character could potentially turn Methuselahs into bugs and kill them by stepping on them because the Methuselahs will gain the Attributes and Health Levels of a bug (they will still have their Abilities, Blood Pool, and Disciplines, so they may be very hard bugs to kill depending on their Discipline spread, but they will have to survive for one scene as a bug)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different effects, but under the same named numina of shapeshifting, yes? Things like that do change between editions. Not really a fan of picking and choosing what I like between editions. Unless you are playing all 1E, in which, as I was curious on, how True Breed worked back then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:17:34-08:00","id":1027742,"title":"","content":"We are already picking and choosing between editions because there is no M20 Sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:34:19-08:00","id":1027748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027742#post1027742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are already picking and choosing between editions because there is no M20 Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't think there is a difference between choosing the most recent rules iteration available (Revised) and just picking whatever you want? That said, V20 The Hunters Hunted II has a numina system for hedge magic to use. Probably a lot more appropriate than 1E, not that I have it to review them. (Doesn't look like it does have a shape-shifting one). I might comb through some other books later to see if there is something else comparable in a non-just sorcerer X20 book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 01-06-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T22:51:06-08:00","id":1028047,"title":"","content":"Off-topic but excited: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027550#post1027550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I had an unresistable urge to stole it. You started a movement.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yessssss! THE PACK ASSEMBLES.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T06:47:53-08:00","id":1028133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1027748#post1027748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you don't think there is a difference between choosing the most recent rules iteration available (Revised) and just picking whatever you want? That said, V20 The Hunters Hunted II has a numina system for hedge magic to use. Probably a lot more appropriate than 1E, not that I have it to review them. (Doesn't look like it does have a shape-shifting one). I might comb through some other books later to see if there is something else comparable in a non-just sorcerer X20 book.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will say the Revised version could have REALLY used some fresh eyes and another week of editing. Summoning, Binding, and Warding was a mess and Anti Psi made no sense as part of the whole. <br /> <br /> I do tend to use similar books like Legos, and build what I need.<br /> <br /> You see this a bit as Wild West and Dark Ages filtered into the modern lines.<br /> <br /> I still patiently wait for Sorcerers &amp; Psychics for WoD20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","user":"EvilTyger","date":". 01-07-2017, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:34:52-08:00","id":1031996,"title":"","content":"another question?<br /> <br /> the Conjuration Numina, how much ritual behaviour or chanting does it require.<br /> <br /> if none I can use it to summon a Ace during a card game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T07:21:26-08:00","id":1032117,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on your paradigm, but it should probably be obvious. You also have to have a prepared object nearby. They have a level two ritual called Sword Summoning though that you could hang, which would allow you to summon a card from miles away, but there are easier ways to cheat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:46:19-08:00","id":1032175,"title":"","content":"any gifts or other numina I could use? <br /> ok for divination.<br /> <br /> reason why someone working as a police officer or bounty hunter would want more then 2 dots, since that gives you dowsing? <br /> <br /> leading to swift finding of a fugitive..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:59:55-08:00","id":1032186,"title":"","content":"I would actually go with the Psychic Numina from Sorcerer: Revised if you wanted to do the supernatural cop routine because they are quick to use and do not require any behaviors that will get you kicked off the force for psychological reasons. Psychometry would give you the name (or face) of the person responsible for a crime, but it would be up to you to find the evidence to make the charges stick in the court of law. Precognition would actually be less useful to a cop (other than Danger Sense) because cops do not exist to prevent crime but to catch people who have already committed a crime (if you spend all of your time as a cop preventing crimes before they occur, you will be quickly on traffic duty because you will not make any arrests).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:29:40-08:00","id":1032402,"title":"","content":"What About daytrading or selling stuff on ebay.<br /> <br /> (Just went into the latter its labor intensive, but lucrative...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user"