night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:09:07-08:00","id":1039031,"title":"","content":"Probably. I just don't think reading any of that will actually help you develop supernatural powers. The same way non of the books from B&amp;N are going to teach you Hedge Magic (imo).<br /> <br /> Actual Supernatural powers should be rare (relatively speaking) imo, and you aren't going to learn them from paperbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:29:43-08:00","id":1039047,"title":"","content":"I agree. If nothing else, entities like the Technocracy are probably really against mortals learning magic outside of their control (strangely enough, everyone else has enough on their plate that they really do not care unless the magic using mortal bothers them). Of course, a group like the Nephandi could potentially print effective books on demon summoning, put up some fake information about it on Amazon and Wikipedia, and uses their mortal pawns to sell the books to used book stores (which are largely outside of the control of entities like the Technocracy). I imagine that they could create large numbers of Infernal Sorcerers with very little work if they played their cards right/ <br /> <br /> What happens when one of the Kinfolk of the Garou starts to dabble with Infernal Sorcery? You can cleanse Wyrm taint from Kinfolk through Gifts and Rites, but can you recover the pieces of a bargained soul the same way? If so, why would a Demon Lord even bargain with one of the Kinfolk? If not, why would a Demon Lord still bargain with one of the Kinfolk if they are just going to be killed by their Garou Kin? Of course, a Demon Lord could require Infernal Sorcerer Kinfolk to purchase the Demonic Investment of the Mask of Innocence during their first commerce of the Soul Trade (after the bonus Paths and Rituals gained from the Greater Pact if the Kinfolk Sorcerer pays the freebie point cost for the Greater Pact on p. 83 of the Hedge Wizard's Handbook).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T15:17:20-08:00","id":1039130,"title":"","content":"Ive bought a few books on tarot lately... its an interesting topic...<br /> <br /> Thought about buying a magic 8 ball or oujia board, to have a larger set of divination stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://