nally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1039231#post1039231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can only imagine the shock some Red Talon might have when they find out one of their lupus kinfolk ancestors was actually a shape shifted homid kinfolk sorcerer. Craig Cobb would have nothing on that freakout.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already possible without adding Sorcerers (or other shape shifters) into the mix. Curse of Lycan or just crossbreeding that just happens because the heart (or other anatomy) wants what it wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:06:41-08:00","id":1039290,"title":"","content":"I think the shock would be greater for it being a Human kinfolk with the Shapechanging Numina, then just having a homid ancestor a few generations back.<br /> <br /> as well as the distrust they'd encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:16:14-08:00","id":1039422,"title":"","content":"Well, Shapeshifters are part of the lore of a lot of families. According to legend, the Plantagenets were supposed to be descended from a daughter of Satan who transformed into a crow when they dragged her into a church. Sounds like they might have been Corax Kin...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T08:45:18-08:00","id":1039437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1039422#post1039422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Shapeshifters are part of the lore of a lot of families. According to legend, the Plantagenets were supposed to be descended from a daughter of Satan who transformed into a crow when they dragged her into a church. Sounds like they might have been Corax Kin...</div> </div> </div> </div>Corax don't just happen, though. Other Corax have to make them happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:03:45-08:00","id":1039444,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, but Corax Kin are produced the standard way. The 'daughter of Satan' may have been Corax produced in the standard fashion, while her children would have been Corax Kin produced in the standard fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:24:04-08:00","id":1039781,"title":"","content":"another question on numina... it said &quot;Kinfolk with True faith in Gaia may be able to affect wyrm creatures, or wyrm tainted individuals&quot; <br /> <br /> how much do you think that would be tappeed by Garou?<br /> <br /> someone who can make a BSD break down on the floor wailing about his own worthlessness is worthy of a bit of respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T20:30:28-08:00","id":1039787,"title":"","content":"Anyone with True Faith is going to be respected (especially if they have True Faith in Gaia, Luna, or Helios).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:41:35-08:00","id":1039830,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> said. It's not like True Faith in Gaia is so alien to the Garou. There was a CoG Chalice (granted, this is from an early book so keep that in mind) that granted a level of Faith when you drank from it.<br /> And the example you gave <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> really is a high level of Faith (5 from memory). That kind of Faith is exceedingly rare, which is saying something since even 1 level is supposed to be incredible rare. More likely the Kinfolk with Faith is going to possibly be able to drive back a Spiral or be immune to their mind altering powers (the lower levels).<br /> <br /> Even that though, if it's known is going to be looked at as a blessing from Gaia, and the kinfolk will be treated as such.<br /> <br /> Editing to add: The &quot;if it's known though&quot; is really important. Most True Faith effects are supposed to be subtle. Even someone with enough Faith (1) to push a Spiral back, will probably then get a pipe thrown at their head and die from that afterwards. Nothing about Faith stops that sort of retaliation once you move back. In any case, there is a decent chance that the kinfolk never realizes their full potential, and that the Garou don't discover it either. Now granted, that's a boring approach to take. But I feel it's perfectly in line with the WoD setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-29-2017, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T07:53:54-08:00","id":1039986,"title":"","content":"You know, the Garou would probably think that Kinfolk with medium levels of True Faith (3-5) were a type of Kami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:36:22-08:00","id":1040002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1039986#post1039986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the Garou would probably think that Kinfolk with medium levels of True Faith (3-5) were a type of Kami.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming it's True Faith in something that's amenable to Gaian causes. Also, I wish that there could be reconciliation between the two different systems used for TF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:56:21-08:00","id":1040015,"title":"","content":"how will a dancer react to the memory of being seized by feelings of absolute WORTHLESSNESS and kneeling like a dog begging for forgiveness or death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:17:15-08:00","id":1040028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1040015#post1040015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how will a dancer react to the memory of being seized by feelings of absolute WORTHLESSNESS and kneeling like a dog begging for forgiveness or death.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a very strange view on how True Faith works. First you seem to only be quoting True Faith 5, as if that's the standard True Faith (it isn't) and even then, you are treating it as an offensive power. Said Dancer won't suffer how you portray it, unless it's trapped with the Faithful (which isn't likely, given the Umbral escape route).<br /> <br /> This is what I could find for True Faith 5: &quot;The person is so pure, so holy, that they can fill a vampire with self-loathing, disgust, terror, and even physical pain. Any vampire hearing the person pray, preach, or recite psalms, or who is touched by the faithful, may be forced to flee immediately. A vampire who is unable to flee is reduced to a gibbering wreck, flailing on the floor and screaming, sobbing, or begging forgiveness. To avoid fleeing, the vampire must either expend one Willpower point per turn or make a Stamina roll each turn (difficulty of 5 + their own Intelligence) \u2014 the higher the vampire\u2019s Intelligence, the higher the difficulty, as the more tortured and guilty they feel.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, for this, we will replace &quot;vampire&quot; with &quot;Spiral&quot;.<br /> So the Dancer spends a Willpower to not flee <u>or</u> rolls Stamina at dif 7-8 (relatively easy for a Garou). Again, you seem to be treating Faith as offensive power. If you look at the systems it fails outright, even if you do manage to have this theoretical Kinfolk with True Faith 5. That kinfolk will be much better served far away from enemies, inspiring their own warriors. If they end up in combat, they are only slightly less likely to end up dead than a kinfolk without Faith facing a BSD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:43:51-08:00","id":1040051,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> another question.<br /> <br /> ideas where on the renown chart, an empathic healer who returned a broken hero one more whole to the sept, by absorbing his Harano into themselves, should Fall?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:50:35-08:00","id":1040056,"title":"","content":"Yeah, True Faith really is not an offensive ability (especially not against any Fera). Personally, I like the True Faith from Dark Ages: Vampire (p. 288-289) because it is can be customized. True Faith increases the difficulty of any supernatural power against its possessor's heart, mind, or soul by its level and increases the Conscience die pool of its possessor by its level (it also makes the blood of its possessor less palatable to Kindred and, at level 3 or greater, poisonous to Kindred). With each level (including the first level), its possessors can choose one additional effect (Blessing, Exorcism, Healing Touch, The Sight, or Warding).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:15:40-08:00","id":1040134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1040051#post1040051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ideas where on the renown chart, an empathic healer who returned a broken hero one more whole to the sept, by absorbing his Harano into themselves, should Fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honor 2, Wisdom 2? Just a ballpark guess after looking at the kinfolk Renown chart. Outside of dying for a Caern, 4 points is about the highest it goes for any single thing. Maybe 3 Honor, 1 Wisdom. Possibly reward 5 points total (split between the 2) if the Garou in question is particularly important.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Kinfolk will be treated highly regardless of actual Renown gain, and the Garou in question will certainly own them. Not everything in Werewolf is measures in points on a sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:11:08-08:00","id":1040164,"title":"","content":"I always imagined renown for kinfolk is very much Sept dependent. Bill the kinfolk is treated with great respect in the Sept of Lady's Crossing, but outside of that Sept, Bill is a nobody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:15:18-08:00","id":1040170,"title":"","content":"Well, if you receive Renown, your actions are known throughout the Garou Nation and the Middle Umbra, since Renown is a spiritual trait as well as a social trait. For Kinfolk to receive Renown, they have to do something that gets the attention of both the Garou Nations and the Middle Umbra. Of course, Kinfolk probably have to have Renown before most Spirits will agree to teach them Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T20:51:09-08:00","id":1041091,"title":"","content":"another reason to prefer Numina... though... if Im in Black eagle and want to be able to keep my allys combat ready I'd DEFINITELY prefer Eves Touch to Healing or Empathic Healing Numina.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T21:56:04-08:00","id":1041103,"title":"","content":"Or Psychic Healing, though the combination of Eve's Touch and Psychic Healing would be quite effective. You could use Eve's Touch to stabilize people and Psychic Healing to bring them back to health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T11:59:00-08:00","id":1041378,"title":"","content":"oh another thing<br /> <br /> Psychic vampirism vs soulstealing, how do they compare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:29:48-08:00","id":1041404,"title":"","content":"Psychic Vampirism is much better than Soul-Stealing in my opinion because Psychic Vampirism is more flexible and does not cost Willpower. With Psychic Vampirism 3, you can steal bashing health levels and use them to heal and, when you are healed, change them to two points of Willpower each. With Psychic Vampirism 4, you can steal lethal health levels and use them to heal bashing health levels, lethal health levels, or use them to downgrade aggravated damage to lethal damage and, when you are healed, change them to three points of Willpower each. Of course, you can do different things with Soul-Stealing than Psychic Vampirism (such as boosting Health Levels with level 4 and stealing Gnosis with level 5), but I would rather have Psychic Vampirism myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:36:50-08:00","id":1042279,"title":"","content":"What about Telepathic control vs Psychic hypnosis.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts on those two?<br /> <br /> I still think a monkey wrencher with psychic hypnosis could do all kinds of stuff to pentex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:12:13-08:00","id":1042292,"title":"","content":"Sure. The thing about Psychic Hypnosis is that it is 'fire-and-forget' while Telepathic Control is 'remote control'. The subject can spend a point of Willpower to ignore a command from Telepathic Control, allowing them a turn to call for help or sabotage your actions (like throwing away the pistol or jumping off a ledge), but they do not have that ability with Psychic Hypnosis. Of course, Telepathic Control takes a turn while Psychic Hypnosis takes minutes, so they both have their place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T19:54:41-08:00","id":1048042,"title":"","content":"oh on those 2 powers?<br /> <br /> ideas on how to make effective use of them at lower levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T20:00:43-08:00","id":1048045,"title":"","content":"Telepathic Control is difficult to make useful at level 1 but level 2 can force a subject to pull a trigger or close their eyes. Psychic Hypnosis 1 and 2 are mostly for entertainment value, though a clever PC could find some use for level 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:46:39-08:00","id":1048746,"title":"","content":"oh on the flip side.<br /> <br /> ideas how a garou can defend from Numina, say a hedge witch places a curse, or a member of the SAD with astral projection decides to stroll around a sept and spy.<br /> <br /> or sends in a spy using animal control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:11:29-08:00","id":1048775,"title":"","content":"Well, Astral Projection is related to the High Umbra, so there are difficulties with preventing that sort of spying (though SAD does not seem to have that ability). When targeted by curses, Fera get a Willpower roll to throw off the effect if they become aware of the curse. Other than that, Fera and Kinfolk can learn Numina, though Fera are usually better off learning their own Gifts (except for countermagic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T11:30:04-08:00","id":1048839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1048746#post1048746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ideas how a garou can defend from Numina, say a hedge witch places a curse,</div> </div> </div> </div>Curses can generally be removed via spirit interference. All of the things that fall into a vague category of how to handle them will usually fall back to the catch-all of &quot;spirits&quot; for a solution. There is next to nothing humans can inflict that spirits can't undo. It's just a matter of finding the right spirit and convincing (paying/bribing) it to help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1048746#post1048746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or a member of the SAD with astral projection decides to stroll around a sept and spy.<br /> <br /> or sends in a spy using animal control.</div> </div> </div> </div>SAD doesn't have this ability, but overlooking that atm...this is a problem with the setting as written when you include any of the other splats. When you come to crossovers, all of the Supernaturals have this weakness. Because the games weren't designed with the other games in mind, most of the Supernaturals have their own designated spirit worlds that others can't (or have a hard time trying to) affect. That means Caerns can be Astrally projected into (by Mages, and Sorcerers/Psychics and Vampires) with zero defense (Ghosts also get to wander in and out). Vampire Chantries (and Mages ones too a lot of the time) can be entered via the Umbra with little defense (Ghosts work here too a lot of the time). Haunts tend to be the safest, but mostly because they're located on another plane altogether.<br /> And slightly different, but this same issue comes up with animal spies. Every Supernatural gets to use them, and so why each group doesn't know about the inner workings of the others because of this also needs to be sorted out.<br /> <br /> It is just a problem with the setting as written. You have to come up with some logical answer for your own WoD for why this doesn't work this way. It's kind of stupid all in all.<br /> <br /> So yes, as written Astral Projection and/or animal spies will get you whatever information you need from Caerns (and any/most Supernatural fortresses) in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T11:55:20-08:00","id":1048851,"title":"","content":"Well, one possible reason why people do not have all of the answers is the rarity of supernatural creatures. While lesser supernatural creatures in totality may be uncommon, greater supernatural creatures in totality are rare. Targeting the right person, even if they do not have supernatural defenses, is nearly impossible just through random selection (something on the order of 0.01% of the global population are greater supernatural, and half of that population is defended by the Mists).<br /> <br /> Greater supernatural creatures also usually have some sort of gimmick that protects them from mundane perception (the Delirium for Fera and Possessed, the Fog for Wraiths, and the Mists for Changelings and Chimera). Especially in the case of the Mists, it is very easy for everyone to forget that they dealt with Changelings or Chimera within a few minutes after witnessing them in the Fae Mien (this is even true for supernatural creatures, which is a mixed blessing when Changelings or Chimera are trying to find allies that they do not have to Enchant). In the case of the Delirium or the Fog, 86% of the mortal population will forget that they encountered the greater supernatural creature and another 12% of the mortal population will rationalize the experience, meaning that only 2% of the population will accurately remember the event (and their associates will think that they are insane when they talk about ghosts or werewolves). A Sorcerer would find it exceptionally hard to convince their superiors that greater supernatural entities exist (perhaps with the exception of Mages and Vampires) just because their superiors are cognitively incapable of remembering if they witnessed supernatural events.<br /> <br /> For example, the average FBI agent has a Willpower of 6 and possesses no Occult Knowledge, so he will be Conciliatory when affected by the Delirium and the Fog, and he will forget the events minutes after they happen. Since he will most likely forget or rationalize the events after they occur, the majority of greater supernatural creatures will probably not bother to kill him, as dead (or missing) government agents tend to bring around people asking uncomfortable questions. An FBI agent affected by the Delirium will beg for his life but, after the Garou finishes her mission and leaves, will forget the encounter and will report the massacre or sabotage to his superiors as if he just stumbled upon the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T12:32:53-08:00","id":1048872,"title":"","content":"That still only addresses human interactions with the Supernatural. The setting doesn't work as written because the various major Supernaturals have undefendable means of spying on one another (and they certainly at least have idea on where the others are located). And for the most part, I was leaving Changelings out of it, because they are unique in more than a few ways (they are the most populous earthbound Supernatural and the Mists leave little room for remembering because of how Banality isn't tied to any increasable trait, and their Freeholds are generally outside of the reach of any/most Supernatural powers).<br /> <br /> Animal spies can be used against all earthly Supernatural fortresses (Caerns, Chantries, Havens) with little way to defend against them. Projection offers a backdoor into those places. Ghosts get to go pretty much wherever they want (with only specific Ghost targeting Wards working against them, and even those are bypassable with some creative uses of Arcanoi). The Umbra serves as a backdoor into most places. The only reason Mage Chantries get to be even somewhat defensible is because of the Ritual casting game mechanics (generally added together with OOC knowledge being sprinkled into Mage defense setups).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T13:13:03-08:00","id":1048901,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that is why Sorcerers end up being the backbone of the supernatural community. They can create wards against practically anything, and they probably do not ask too many questions about who their customers are or why they need specific wards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T13:40:43-08:00","id":1048910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1048901#post1048901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that is why Sorcerers end up being the backbone of the supernatural community. They can create wards against practically anything, and they probably do not ask too many questions about who their customers are or why they need specific wards.</div> </div> </div> </div>With no insult intended (and I mean that entirely sincerely) your version of the WoD seems to have very little in common with the WoD as written in the books.<br /> <br /> In this case, you've taken a minor Splat group and made them integral for every &quot;major&quot; Supernatural to function. Which is really odd, imo. There is really no shot that Garou would call in Sorcerers to set up protections around their Caerns (and they shouldn't <i>have to</i>). Same goes for Vampires I would think (not without said Sorcerers being thoroughly controlled).<br /> <br /> So yea, this is a possible solution, but I don't think it really works since is somehow makes all of the major players reliant on unique defenses only this outside group can provide. It could work for a unique city setup (and even then it strains belief), but it really falls apart when you try and implement is on a grand scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:32:46-08:00","id":1048939,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk Sorcerers would not be called in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:37:48-08:00","id":1049074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1048939#post1048939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk Sorcerers would not be called in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no, almost certainly not. Not in the WoD as written.<br /> <br /> for 2 reasons, off the top of my head:<br /> 1) kinfolk Sorcerers are rare. And there is no certainty they have the Paths necessary.<br /> 2) it isn't their job. There are Rites specifically to protect Caerns. Those Rites should be enough, since they're what's written into the setting. If there were easy ways around them, then that makes them pointless and so different/better Rites would have been developed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:55:15-08:00","id":1049155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049074#post1049074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> for 2 reasons, off the top of my head:<br /> 1) kinfolk Sorcerers are rare. And there is no certainty they have the Paths necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you<i> trying</i> to bait a discussion of kinfolk sorcerer population ratios? Pls no.<br /> C'mon man. You're better than this. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:54:49-08:00","id":1049231,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think the answer would range from 'indeterminate' to 'unavailable', and every ST would have a different number. For example, I have Garou Human Kinfolk with a population equal to 100 times the Garou population (1:5,000). Of that population, 15% are Sorcerers (equally divided between Mythical, Psychic, and Technological), with 80% being dabblers and 20% being practitioners (meaning that Garou Human Kinfolk Practitioners would have a population of 1:500,000 for each of Mythic, Psychic, and Technological). In my games, that means that there are three Kinfolk Sorcerer Practitioners (one Mythic, one Psychic, and one Trchnological) for every Garou.<br /> <br /> But that is just in my games, and every ST is going to use different numbers. STs that run higher Garou populations would need less Kinfolk Sorcerer Practitioners to take up the slack. With a fivefold increase in Garou populations, Kinfolk Sorcerer Practitioners are practically unneeded by the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T05:32:45-08:00","id":1049250,"title":"","content":"Hmnn should kinfolk sorcerers more often learn from the new age section of a bookstore.<br /> <br /> or through being apprenticed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T06:45:44-08:00","id":1049275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049155#post1049155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you<i> trying</i> to bait a discussion of kinfolk sorcerer population ratios? Pls no.<br /> C'mon man. You're better than this. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>...I know. Sorry. And I'm not actually trying to get into that discussion. I was trying to give a quick response to what seemed like a quick question.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, those numbers are...bizarre. You have Garou (in the Garou Nation) outnumbered by practicing (not even your &quot;dabblers&quot;) Sorcerers at a 3:1 ratio. That just makes it the Sorcerer Nation with some Garou warriors sprinkled in. Those numbers fundamentally alter the setting as written.<br /> I am curious when you decided that Sorcerers were such a prevalent force in the WoD (outnumbering everyone but Wraiths and Changelings). This seems to have been a running theme for you on the forums only recently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049250#post1049250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmnn should kinfolk sorcerers more often learn from the new age section of a bookstore.<br /> <br /> or through being apprenticed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The New Age section of a bookstore should not be able to offer any real magic. None. You should not be able to go to B&amp;N for an hour and come out knowing how to change the weather or how to summon up Hellfire.<br /> <br /> So I suppose this is a vote for Apprenticeship. I think that's how the overwhelming majority of Sorcerers in the WoD learn their magic, with a very small number of them stumbling across real arcane writings that can actually impart the knowledge needed to learn or advance Paths. Real magic (even a dot or 2) should in no way be commonplace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:00:21-08:00","id":1049299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049275#post1049275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The New Age section of a bookstore should not be able to offer any real magic. None. You should not be able to go to B&amp;N for an hour and come out knowing how to change the weather or how to summon up Hellfire.<br /> <br /> So I suppose this is a vote for Apprenticeship. I think that's how the overwhelming majority of Sorcerers in the WoD learn their magic, with a very small number of them stumbling across real arcane writings that can actually impart the knowledge needed to learn or advance Paths. Real magic (even a dot or 2) should in no way be commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's complicated, one might say there's a bit of both things in WoD, reinforced in no small measure by many bits and pieces of fluff in both editions of the book itself and/or hints in Ascension about Acolytes &amp; such, sort of leaving in the air and up to ST fiat if hedge wizards/linear magicians/sorcerers are less, just as or more common than any one particular brand of major supernatural.<br /> <br /> That said, <b>even</b> if they were actually more numerous than <b>all supers put together</b>, they are also far more fragmented, disperse or outright fractious overall, with a much greater number of cults, esoteric societies, fraternities and so on to join, mix up, confront and overall interact with, not having the loose unity and range of clans/tribes/traditions by even the longest of shoots. No elders/methuselahs, rank 5-6, archmages/oracles or whatever to order and direct <b>that</b> particular herd of cats... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-15-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:46:57-08:00","id":1049311,"title":"","content":"No, I have always thought that Sorcerers as a group are an important part of cWoD, even if they are not individually important, I just have not focused on it much until recently. As for the Garou Nation, what does it matter to Garou if Kinfolk Sorcerer outnumber them? They are just support personnel, they are not combat personnel, but Garou should want competent support personnel. I see Kindred feeling the same way about Ghoul Sorcerers. I agree about the lack of organization among Sorcerers, though each Garou Tribe or Kindred Clan might impose some organization on their dependent Sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-15-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:31:56-08:00","id":1049361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049299#post1049299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's complicated, one might say there's a bit of both things in WoD, reinforced in no small measure by many bits and pieces of fluff in both editions of the book itself and/or hints in Ascension about Acolytes &amp; such, sort of leaving in the air and up to ST fiat if hedge wizards/linear magicians/sorcerers are less, just as or more common than any one particular brand of major supernatural.<br /> <br /> That said, <b>even</b> if they were actually more numerous than <b>all supers put together</b>, they are also far more fragmented, disperse or outright fractious overall, with a much greater number of cults, esoteric societies, fraternities and so on to join, mix up, confront and overall interact with, not having the loose unity and range of clans/tribes/traditions by even the longest of shoots. No elders/methuselahs, rank 5-6, archmages/oracles or whatever to order and direct <b>that</b> particular herd of cats... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. But this is why I closed my statement with &quot;this is a vote for Apprenticeship&quot; as opposed to saying this is just the setting as written. I acknowledge that is purely my opinion (though I do think it is supported by the books) instead of saying that it is a black and white answer to the question given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049311#post1049311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for the Garou Nation, what does it matter to Garou if Kinfolk Sorcerer outnumber them? They are just support personnel, they are not combat personnel, but Garou should want competent support personnel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way you describe it, they become a lot more than &quot;support personnel&quot; if the Garou <i>need</i> them to set up defenses for their Caerns (which also serves to enforce the idea that Garou can't take care of their own Caerns). Kinfolk as written are already competent. They don't need supernatural powers to upgrade their importance. That distorts their thematic purpose imo.<br /> <br /> And mind you, I do agree that there is probably a higher percentage of Sorcerers among kinfolk compared to &quot;regular&quot; humans. I just don't think it's anywhere near the level that you have them be at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049311#post1049311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see Kindred feeling the same way about Ghoul Sorcerers. I agree about the lack of organization among Sorcerers, though each Garou Tribe or Kindred Clan might impose some organization on their dependent Sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of &quot;their&quot; Sorcerers is one that strikes me as odd. As if each Supernatural group (well Garou and Vampires at least) has a stable of Sorcerers to call on. If that were the case, then I think it would have been mentioned in the books somewhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:39:45-08:00","id":1049362,"title":"","content":"Well, Ghoul Sorcerers are probably less common than Kinfolk Sorcerers because Ghouls are probably less common than Kinfolk. Garou and Kinfolk have to have carpenters, electricians, plumbers, etc too, but they do not discuss the necessity of Ghoul or Kinfolk electricians in the books either because they are just support staff. Ghoul and Kinfolk Sorcerers would just be seen as another form of skilled labor by Garou and Kindred (it is not like Garou and Kindred disbelieve the existence of magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:48:42-08:00","id":1049368,"title":"","content":"On that was wondering, does a sorcerers day job have to mesh with his Field of study<br /> <br /> A doctor knowing H ealing,<br /> <br /> A Detective knowing Divination<br /> <br /> Someone not at all citified knowing Herbalism.<br /> <br /> Any more examples?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:37:18-08:00","id":1049388,"title":"","content":"Dabblers could develop anything that caught their interest because Numina would be more of an exotic hobby than a magical vocation (like people who take martial arts classes twice a week). Practitioners would probably create a day job around their Numina because Numina would be a magical vocation rather than an exotic hobby (like people who spend four hours a day practicing martial arts so they can be professional MMA fighters). So a Detective Practitioner might have Alchemy (so she can create potions to improve her capabilities), Conjuration (so she can avoid ever being unarmed), Divination (so she could read the future), Enchantment (so she can create talismans to improve her capabilities), or Fascination (so she can manipulate people).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:13:50-08:00","id":1049477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049362#post1049362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Garou and Kinfolk have to have carpenters, electricians, plumbers, etc too, but they do not discuss the necessity of Ghoul or Kinfolk electricians in the books either because they are just support staff. Ghoul and Kinfolk Sorcerers would just be seen as another form of skilled labor by Garou and Kindred</div> </div> </div> </div>You are comparing real magic to having a dot or 2 in a skill. Those aren't the same. A better comparison would be a kinfolk with a dot or 2 of Rituals or Occult, since that would be comparing Abilities. I think your (my understanding of what you've said) view that being able to cast spells is the same (or even similar) to the skillset needed to fix a toilet is where we have a disconnect in this conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1049368#post1049368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that was wondering, does a sorcerers day job have to mesh with his Field of study</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, though if they have more than a few levels of a Path, they would have had to devote years of study to it so it is unlikely that they're professional career should be far off from their Sorcerer focus.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:07:27-08:00","id":1049812,"title":"","content":"Any ideas how to justify a Diviner working as a fortune teller, rather a bounty hunter or daytrader?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:24:18-08:00","id":1049818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1022430-kinfolk-sorcerers?p=1048910#post1048910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With no insult intended (and I mean that entirely sincerely) your version of the WoD seems to have very little in common with the WoD as written in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, I believe he also has anyone in the Camarilla be able to learn Bardo. No offense intended to Aya, but I've very often found his perception of WoD to be different than most.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:02:16-08:00","id":1049850,"title":"","content":"If you have lower levels of Divination, you lack the accuracy to be a successful daytrader. At level 4 or 5 though, you should be quite wealthy. In general, I think that Sorcerers should have a minimum Resources of (Divination/Fortune - 2) unless they have a real good reason not to be wealthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:26:42-08:00","id":1049890,"title":"","content":"one problem I have with using the Sorcerer Numina, is a lot of them are FAR more powerful then the ones in kinfolk and hunters hunted<br /> <br /> Who wants to take Cursing from hunters Hunted II when fortune exists.<br /> <br /> or Kinfolk unsung heroes Divination when Sorcerer Divination exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:49:19-08:00","id":1049902,"title":"","content":"Of course, that was part of the corrections that occurred with Revised. Fortune is Cursing, Divination is Divination, etc. The only older versions that are interesting are the old Ephemera and the old Shapeshifting because they offer equal but different versions of their equivalent powers in Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:26:37-08:00","id":1049956,"title":"","content":"Or the various versions of powers were never written with a complete crossover in mind. HH version of Paths are what there are in Vampire, and Kinfolk (both versions) had their own versions. And Sorcerer was a Mage specific book, even if it was easily used for crossover. But the Kinfolk and HH Paths weren't meant to be compared to Sorcerer Revised. Also, Hunters Hunted II is part of the V20 line, and so it is more updated (and therefore should supersede) than Sorcerer Revised.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:00:37-08:00","id":1050007,"title":"","content":"at 2 dots of Divination you may not be ready to daytrade... but should be ready for bounty hunting.<br /> <br /> But even if a fortune teller knows a dot or 2 of divination, they may 